    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for the owner telephone E.164 rule in `OwnerTelephone.java` \u2014 the single source of truth shared by `ValidateOwnerFields` (normalizes the submitted value \u2192 400 on reject) and `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java:toE164`):\n- Added a `NATIONAL_LENGTH` map of country calling code \u2192 required national digits (`\"61\"` \u2192 9, `\"1\"` \u2192 10), ordered longest-code-first so a longer code is matched before a shorter prefix.\n- After the existing 8\u201315 digit check, the code now matches the leading country code and verifies the remaining national digits are exactly the required length, returning `null` (\u2192 400) when they are not. Country codes outside the map keep only the generic 8\u201315 bound, so existing behavior is preserved.\n\nThe rule stays idempotent (re-running on an already-normalized `+61\u2026`/`+1\u2026` value passes), so the uniqueness comparison in `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` is unaffected.\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The new acceptance test `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (`+61 123` \u2192 400) passes, and the `uniqueTelephone()` fixture (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 national digits) remains valid across the whole pipeline.",
